>> title: Hungarian Goulash
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, paprika, hungarian, one-pot, stew
>> counters: Deli, Diner, One Pot
>> aka: gulyás, gulyas, beef goulash
>> servings: 6
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: narrow — the paprika scorches about thirty seconds after it goes in, and nothing in the two and a half hours after takes it back
>> step.3: stir in
>> step.4: simmer covered 2 hr
>> step.5: simmer 30 min more

Render @lard{2%Tbs}, @yellow onions{2%lb}(900 g; thinly sliced) in a heavy #pot{} until deep golden.

Bloom @Hungarian sweet paprika{1/4%cup}(30 g; stirred in off the heat so it does not scorch), @caraway seed{1%tsp}, @garlic{4%cloves}(minced) in @&(~1)onions{}.

Stir @beef chuck{3%lb}(1.4 kg; cut in 1-in cubes), @kosher salt{1%Tbs} into @&(~1)paprika base{}.

Simmer @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{4%cup}(950 mL), @tomato{1%large}(chopped), @green pepper{1}(chopped) for ~{2%hr}.

Add @Yukon Gold potatoes{1%lb}(450 g; cut in 1-in cubes) to @&(~1)goulash{} for ~{30%min}.
